ResPre: contact map prediction using Deep Residual network and Precision matrix 

1.Getting Started
	python respre.py [msa_file] [outfile]
		msa_file: Multiple Sequence Alignment file
		outfile:  Output file, each line in this format: [position1 position2 score]
		where position index start from 1 [NOT 0]
	

2.Prerequisites
	Python numpy and scipy should be installed.
	Please install pytorch-0.3.0 first[http://pytorch.org/]
		by 'conda install pytorch torchvision -c pytorch' if you have conda installed
		you can check pytorch version by 'import torch \n torch.__version__'
	There is an exe file under 'bin' path, Maybe you also need to 'chmod' exe permission to the exe file.

3.Example
	You can test by fowllowing commands:
		' python respre.py test/T0759-D1.aln test/T0759-D1.out '
	It will generate 2 files:
		' T0759-D1.out.weight ': Weights for each sequence in msa, you can just ignore it.
		' T0759-D1.out '       : Output file 
		
4.Performence
	Comparing with DeepCov on 158 non-redundant test set using same MSAs:
			long-range:topL		long-range:topL/5 		all-range:topL		all-range:topL/5
	DeepCov		37.84				64.23					56.58				78.58
	DeepPRE		48.04				70.72					65.83				83.98
	respre		49.70				72.08					68.22				85.54
	
5.Built With
	python numpy scipy pytorch 
	This tool is only tested under python3.5/3.6. Contact me if you have any problems.
	
